{"parentUuid":"d316704f-727f-4109-9a13-70c488f552d2","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-14","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"feat/fontkit","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01HX42uMRvfkYrsOGZrdWlB2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your laptop has GOPRIVATE=git.quillmark.example/* in its go env file (set once with go env -w), which is why it works for you. GOPRIVATE tells Go not to use the public proxy and not to ask the checksum database for matching modules; it sets the defaults of GONOPROXY and GONOSUMDB. The CI job has no GOPRIVATE, so it asks sum.golang.org. The proxy fallback to direct already worked thanks to the git credentials the job sets up, so the checksum lookup is the only thing missing.\n\nThe fix is to set GOPRIVATE in the workflow env of the build job, and to add the go env -w step to CONTRIBUTING.md for new machines."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":394,"output_tokens":114}},"uuid":"b8338dc5-54dc-45aa-9334-18f25668e1f8","timestamp":"2026-09-24T09:32:24.000Z","requestId":"req_011CZZe94S5nIfAvIcLIe3w1"}
